SlopOS handoff diagnostics: boot every entry as the menu editor would

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
A derivative of Limine (BSD-2-Clause, see COPYING in its tree), not part of
upstream Limine. Applies on top of 0001-slopos-handoff-diagnostics.patch;
`scripts/build_limine_diag.sh --autoboot-as-editor` applies both.

Pressing e and then F10 with nothing changed boots where Enter, the timeout
and a one-shot boot do not. On those paths, before boot(), this does what the
editor path does that they lack: it keeps a copy of the entry in an
editor-sized buffer and boots from it, allocates and frees the editor's cell
map, and drains the pointer devices with mouse_flush(). Allocations from
boot() on then land where an edited boot's do, and the pointer protocols are
left as the editor leaves them. The header line says AUTOBOOT-AS-EDITOR and
MIMIC=1 when it ran. -DSLOPOS_DIAG_MIMIC_NO_ALLOC (mouse_flush only) or
-DSLOPOS_DIAG_MIMIC_NO_FLUSH (allocations only) builds one half, to tell
which of the two an edited boot needs.

